# Blank — UI structure

Minimal app shell with the **full `internal/ui` registry tree** for staging reusable UI.
On-disk index: **`internal/ui/README.md`** (same `registry:*` labels as FastyGoUI).

```
internal/ui/
  layout/       # registry:layout — document/chrome shells
                #   shell.templ          (topnav app shell)
                #   sidebar_shell.templ  (topnav + desktop aside slot)
  components/   # registry:components
                #   icon/ toggles/ navigation/ appsidebar/
  blocks/       # registry:blocks — dashboard/, marketing/, docs/ (full scaffolds)
  widgets/      # registry:widgets — UI + behavior (staging)
  variants/     # registry:variants — wireframe utility maps
  utils/        # registry:utils — app helpers on templ/utils
internal/views/
  *.templ       # route pages — each composes its own layout shell
  partials/     # shell head assets, header trailing glue
  models.go     # LayoutData, *PageData (with Shell / Sidebar fields)
  layout_helpers.go # ShellPropsFor, SidebarPropsFor
internal/site/
  router.go     # PageSpec route manifest (no Layout field — pages compose their own)
  render.go     # handlePage, web.Render (one call, no wrapping adapter)
  nav.go        # nav from route specs
  layout_data.go # LayoutData, language switch, assets
  feature.go    # Feature wiring only
internal/fixtures/
  locale/*.json # i18n copy
```

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/ui/layout` | Document chrome and named shells (`Shell`, `SidebarShell`); stays in app |
| `internal/ui/components` | Props-only UI; no HTTP or fetch |
| `internal/ui/components/appsidebar` | Local sidebar component used as `SidebarShell`'s aside slot |
| `internal/ui/blocks/<domain>/` | Full scaffolds (future `fastygo/blocks`); **not** for empty 4-line adapters |
| `internal/ui/widgets` | Behavior shells → future `fastygo/widgets` |
| `internal/views` | Pages only — each composes `@layout.Shell { ... }` or `@layout.SidebarShell(..., aside) { ... }` |
| `internal/site` | Runtime routing; not a registry |

**Page composes layout.** Open `views/<route>.templ` and you see the full tree: `@layout.Shell { content }` or `@layout.SidebarShell(shell, appsidebar.AppSidebar(s)) { content }`. There are **no** `views/*Shell` route-adapter functions.

**Named shells in `internal/ui/layout/`:**
- `layout.Shell` — topnav document chrome (`html + head + body + Header + main{children} + Footer`).
- `layout.SidebarShell` — same chrome plus a desktop aside slot beside the main column.

Add new shells in `internal/ui/layout/` only when a route needs structurally different document chrome. Geometry variants (alternate sidebars, dashboard grids, docs toc shells) belong as **full scaffolds** in `internal/ui/blocks/<domain>/<organism>/`, not empty adapter wrappers.

**Forbidden:**
- `internal/ui/recipes`, `internal/ui/elements`, `internal/ui/ui/`, `internal/ui/blocks/layout/`.
- 4-line `blocks/*` packages that only call `@layout.Shell { @body }`.
- `views/*Shell` adapter functions that forward props with no markup.

**views** receive resolved strings/structs only — no `fixtures.LoadLocale` inside `.templ`.

When adding a page:

1. Extend `fixtures.Locale` and every `locale/*.json`.
2. Add `*PageData` in `internal/views/models.go` — include `Shell layout.ShellProps` (and `Sidebar appsidebar.Props` for sidebar pages).
3. Add `internal/views/<page>.templ` — compose `@layout.Shell(data.Shell) { ... }` or `@layout.SidebarShell(data.Shell, appsidebar.AppSidebar(data.Sidebar)) { ... }`.
4. Add one `PageSpec` in `internal/site/router.go` — `Body` returns the page directly (no `Layout` field).

For sidebar layout history, see git branch **`sidebar`**.
